Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 03:13:19 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1186/1265] HERESY 1168: stress marks astray in the lyrics'
 meter; the count composed first; Clear and New song say what they keep
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Viktor, 07.10.2026, the night: «В твой навороченный редактор лирики вшей ещё проверку проёбов с x301. Что не на гласных, в
пустоте, на пробеле... С x301 неправильно считаются слоги, мне так кажется. ע учитывается в слогах как гласная?»

- Every stress mark (U+0301) belongs right after the vowel it stresses (Cyrillic, Latin — his hard o —, Greek, or ע — his
  soft о/а). The meter now finds the ones off a vowel: at a line's start, after a space or a sign, on a consonant, a second
  mark on the same letter, a spacing ´ in its place; and the words with two marks (amber: meant, or a slip?). A button under
  the box counts each kind, lists them in its tip and selects them in turn (a mark with its letter; a lone one with its
  neighbours, to be seen); a mark before the line's count. On his v9.0.9: one, at line 27's start, before «Я».
- The count, measured on his v9.0.9 (89 sung lines) and on 2,033 lines of his recent takes: no line's count moves with its
  stress marks, and ע counts as a vowel. Three faults found instead and mended: a decomposed «й» (и + U+0306, as pasted text
  may bring it) counted as a vowel; a Latin vowel with its acute composed (ó, what «o + U+0301» becomes in a normalizing
  editor) not counted; Belarusian «ў», no syllable, counted. A word is composed (NFC) before it is counted; in English an
  accented vowel counts (café) and a diaeresis parts two (naïve). None of his 2,033 lines counts otherwise.
- Clear's dialog said New song puts the VAE and output back too: it does not, and New song's own dialog said «every knob».
  Both now say what each keeps: Clear the words alone; New song the mode, sampling, sliders and LoRAs as well, Sound and
  output (VAE, solver, steps, length, format) staying. The two changed sentences of New song in all six catalogs; the new
  words English only, for the pass before 2.0.0.

The suite: 374 passed, 0 failed (3 new checks); the F5 clock check waits for the clock to show three seconds instead of a
fixed sleep, which read 0:02 on a busy machine.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
